Begin2
Title        = NEC CDR-260 cd-rom driver
Version      = 0.3 alpha
Desc1        = A prototype driver for the NEC CDR-260 cd-rom drive.
Desc2        = Allows mounting and reading an iso-9660 filesystem.
Desc3        = No audio functions are presently supported.
Desc4        = Should work with devices on either IDE bus.
Desc5        = Driver is built as a loadable module, but requires a few small
Desc6        = kernel patches.  Patches are supplied as diffs against 1.1.50,
Desc7        = but the driver should work with most 1.1 kernels.
Author       = scott snyder
AuthorEmail  = snyder@fnald0.fnal.gov
Maintainer   = scott snyder
MaintEmail   = snyder@fnald0.fnal.gov
Site1        = sunsite.unc.edu
Path1        = /pub/Linux/kernel/patches/cdrom
File1        = nec260-0_3.tgz
FileSize1    = 11265 bytes
Required1    = NEC CDR-260 cd-rom drive, 1.1 kernel, modules utilities
CopyPolicy1  = GPL
Keywords     = cd-rom driver NEC CDR-260
Entered      = 14SEP94
EnteredBy    = scott snyder
CheckedEmail = snyder@fnald0.fnal.gov
End
